# Heard back by N repeaters (phase 3): a channel message we send comes back in the radio log (PUSH_LOG_RX_DATA) over 2 routes, plus one
# copy heard straight from the sender (empty path: not counted). The status says "sent" until the first echo, the count moves while the
# 60 s window is open, then it is final (and saved with the message).
#   SIMARGS="--heard-back 2 --heard-back-direct" SCRIPT=heard-back.script sh ui_smoke.sh
wait 3500
key enter
type hello mesh, who hears me?
key enter
wait 700
say == sent, nothing heard back yet (expect last_status='sent' echoes=1)
dump
shot heard-back-1-sent
wait 1000
say == the copy with an empty path (1 s) is not counted, the first route (1.7 s) is: live count (expect last_status='heard back by 1 repeater')
dump
shot heard-back-2-one
wait 1800
say == the second route, the window is still open (expect last_status='heard back by 2 repeaters' echoes=1)
dump
shot heard-back-3-two
wait 58000
say == the window closed: final (expect last_status='heard back by 2 repeaters' echoes=0)
dump
shot heard-back-4-final
# a direct message is not tracked: it keeps its ack status
key esc
key down
key down
key down
wait 300
key enter
type direct one
key enter
wait 2000
say == a direct message: acks as before, no echo window (expect echoes=0 last_status='delivered')
dump
shot heard-back-5-direct
